Z||000000||Double07||09-13-2000||06:42 PM||||Have a 86 Fiero, v6, 4speed. Oil pressure reads 18 lbs. What should it read?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||09-14-2000||08:59 AM||||Is that at idle or speed? If at idle, what do you read at speed? Try cleaning the connectors at sending unit and checking pressure with a manual gauge.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Double07||09-14-2000||05:19 PM||||20 lbs at speed||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||09-15-2000||12:51 AM||||If I were you, I'd have the pressure checked manually. How many miles? You should have at speed 30 lbs. at least indicated at speed if the gauge is accurate(my personal comfort zone hot). Should you find that you are producing good pressure look into the circut for faults.<p>[This message has been edited by Indiana_resto_guy (edited 09-15-2000).]||||reg||1
